  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "He stands on a mountainside overlooking Gu Yue village, carrying a clan-head letter and orders to investigate the River Swallowing Toad matter while keeping temper and prestige in check on Gu Yue ground. He holds Grand Bear Gu and can erupt with a bear’s strength. Xiong, Gu Yue, and Bai share that mountain under wolf-tide pressure that forces temporary peace among the three villages.",
      "chapters": [
        121
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan",
        "gu_river_swallowing_toad",
        "gu_grand_bear_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Qing Mao Mountain is a small corner of the Southern Border.",
      "chapters": [
        31
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same group includes Xiong Lin as that year’s top Xiong village genius and Xiong Jiang. After beating Chi Shan at the village gate he names Brown Bear Innate Strength Gu and the strength of a bear as the reason Chi Shan still falls short.",
      "chapters": [
        121
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_xiong_lin",
        "loc_xiong_village",
        "char_xiong_jiang",
        "char_chi_shan",
        "gu_brown_bear_innate_strength_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is not as tall as Chi Shan.",
      "chapters": [
        121
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "His two eyes are red. He has bowl-sized fists.",
      "chapters": [
        135
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chi Shan later tells Fang Yuan that Xiong Li has been seeking a strength contest, that Brown Bear Innate Strength Gu already grants one bear’s strength, that Grand Bear Gu can add another, and that the Qing Mao Mountain strongest title belongs to Xiong Li.",
      "chapters": [
        123
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "alliance-contests",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_chi_shan",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At the three-clan alliance gathering Xiong Li’s group beats Bai Bing Yi through Xiong Jiang, then Xiong Li himself challenges Fang Yuan to a strength contest; Fang Yuan admits defeat without fighting.",
      "chapters": [
        125
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "alliance-contests",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bai_bing_yi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He next spars with Gu Yue Qing Shu, breaks only one vine under rising coil strength, and treats Qing Shu as his true rival while dismissing Fang Yuan as a newbie.",
      "chapters": [
        126
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "alliance-contests",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gu_yue_qing_shu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Against Bai Ning Bing he uses Grand Bear Gu at two bears’ strength and is still counted among the rank two elites equal to Qing Shu and Chi Shan while the group is suppressed.",
      "chapters": [
        135
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-fight",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bai_ning_bing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan joins late; Xiong Li lands a heavy punch through a barrier and shows admiration for Fang Yuan’s superb cooperation.",
      "chapters": [
        136
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "wolf-tide-fight",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When a finishing punch is about to land, Bai Ning Bing’s palm blade punctures Xiong Li’s heart, freezes it, and kills him. Xiong Lin and Xiong Jiang cry out as Lord Xiong Li falls.",
      "chapters": [
        137
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later finds the corpse already taken, likely by Xiong Lin, and regrets missing Brown Bear Innate Strength Gu, noting Xiong Li already had a bear’s strength and may have returned that Gu to the clan.",
      "chapters": [
        142
      ],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
